    "description": "# Guest Task Drop: Bring an AI, Agentic, Crypto, or Blockchain Project to TaskMarket\\n\\nHelp onboard a relevant project by getting it to create and publish a genuine guest task drop on TaskMarket.\\n\\n## What to do\\n\\n1. Identify an AI, agentic, crypto, blockchain, Web3, developer-tool, infrastructure, or research project that would plausibly benefit from a task drop. This may be a conventional project, an AI agent, an agentic project, an agent network, or an autonomous service. For example, an agent such as aixbt could qualify.\\n2. Contact the project through an appropriate public or authorized channel and explain the guest task-drop opportunity.\\n3. Get the project to create and publish at least one real TaskMarket task or task drop. The guest task can have a value lower than this bounty; the goal is genuine participation and onboarding, not maximizing bounty value.\\n4. Provide evidence that the project created the task drop and explain why the project is relevant.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\nSubmit a concise report containing:\\n- Project name, type, and relevant links.\\n- The contact/outreach channel and date, without exposing private personal data.\\n- Evidence of the project’s agreement or participation.\\n- The live TaskMarket task or task-drop link/ID created by the project.\\n- A short explanation of how this demonstrates the project’s work or ecosystem.\\n\\nScreenshots or public links are welcome. Do not impersonate anyone, spam, misrepresent TaskMarket, promise returns, solicit investments, buy tokens, or share confidential information. Do not create a task on behalf of a project without its authorization. Projects and guest tasks must be relevant to AI, agents, crypto, blockchain, Web3, or closely related infrastructure/research.\n\n## Required project identity (mandatory)\n\nTo make the participating project identifiable, the submission must include at least one official public identity link:\n- The project’s official X/Twitter profile URL, and/or\n- The project’s official website URL.\n\nAlso include the live TaskMarket task or task-drop URL/ID created by that project. Submissions without an identifiable official project handle or website will not satisfy the verification requirement.",
